{"content": "The release codename mentioned in the comment is **QUARTZ-VELVET-4578**.\n\nThe first class defined in the excerpt, `_ClassFinder`, is an `ast.NodeVisitor` subclass designed to traverse an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) to find a specific class or function definition by its qualified name. It maintains a stack to track the nesting level of classes and functions as it visits nodes, and when it locates a match for the target `qualname`, it raises a custom `ClassFoundException` containing the line number of that definition.", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.30493116994530567, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.30493116994530567}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -1.9574675621572197}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -2.3419089378896416}, {"token": "First", "logprob": -4.5108141960683525}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -4.871474749046868}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -5.214841371971673}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -7.3446669640126885}, {"token": "Release", "logprob": -9.432807451683587}, {"token": "-", "logprob": -9.494370943504876}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -9.98067427297265}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -10.275722986656731}, {"token": "What", "logprob": -10.354893213707513}, {"token": "3", "logprob": -10.381017214256829}, {"token": "<think>", "logprob": -10.438434130150384}, {"token": "```", "logprob": -10.523240572411126}, {"token": "No", "logprob": -10.556759363609856}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -10.618725305992669}, {"token": "based", "logprob": -11.005985743004388}, {"token": "Yes", "logprob": -11.171176439720696}, {"token": "Hello", "logprob": -11.29047537465722}]}, {"token": " release", "logprob": -0.00022386004000551907, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " release", "logprob": -0.00022386004000551907}, {"token": " first", "logprob": -8.47446320940524}, {"token": " code", "logprob": -13.792454466119107}, {"token": " released", "logprob": -13.883902296319302}, {"token": " second", "logprob": -13.985977873101529}, {"token": " spe